  "findings": [
    "All six new blobs inspected including complete contents of four ZIPs. They implement age-based cleanup, ordinary copying or Robocopy mirroring, not byte/hash-confirmed duplicate-file discovery.",
    "deletefiles.ps1 and removelogs/deletelogs.ps1 have deletion pipelines commented out, while log strings still say files have been deleted. The text is not execution proof; no deletion or network drive operation was performed.",
    "deletefiles.ps1 assigns b only inside its allowed-item condition but writes the log outside it. An excluded later entry can log stale b from a previous iteration. This is a source-level state/reporting issue, not a reproduced PowerShell result.",
    "backupsolution.ps1 and FileBackup copy into date-named destinations and lack post-copy content verification or snapshot checks. FileBackup ZIP retention uses CreationTime and active Remove-Item, independent of content equality; no retention task was invoked.",
    "SyncRobocopy starts child processes with source/destination arguments composed from CSV. robocopy.zip adds quoting in its VBS launcher, while the batch file forwards positional arguments. No runtime path-with-spaces or process completion test conducted.",
    "Embedded Robocopy logs are historical samples, not new benchmark or validation evidence. Their status and speed lines must not be counted as current-run results.",
    "No file matcher or production code adopted from this batch; filename/age/mirror status do not establish content identity."
  ],
